{
  "recorded_at_utc": "2026-09-13T05:36:55.4355157Z",
  "status": "0.79.14 OPEN: shared native visible statistics integrated; hardware/software cursor remains open.",
  "release": "0.79.13",
  "nvidia": "0.1.98",
  "kernel": "0.1.162",
  "scope": "Ordinary double/triple-buffer Present now publishes coherent bounded per-head metadata through the common display owner and optional R4DRAW read API. Acquire, CE completion, admitted Window flip, proven visible activation and old-image FINISHED remain distinct; existing CPU/common-copy fences retain their meaning.",
  "binding": "Real post-init display entry and stall vector, distinct from GSP; actual RM head count and active mode head. No PCI scan, second MSI setup, new kernel/ABI or change to default passive bootfb. Normal GSP-only paths remain intact.",
  "concurrency": "Serialized NVIDIA worker publishes only changed metadata; no per-frame log. Generic display state owner stores at most eight head records with no callback, BO operation or wait under its lock. Output copy occurs after unlock. Busy retries; permanent reporting error disables reporting without changing video. Stop/fault adds Lost where the bound display generation remains current.",
  "failure": "One CE job, one ready image and one Window flip are bounded by existing deadlines and common depth-one queue. Busy leaves queued work pending; invalid extents finish failed without visibility. Missing FINISHED while the third CE is submitted causes lost/quarantine retaining all image uses and the unacknowledged source read lease. General copy jobs wait for the outstanding flip; mode/catalog/table work cannot enter during Present.",
  "diagnostics": "DISPLAYD /STATS [head-id] reads the latest snapshot without device calls or Present. Shows configured buffers, pending operations, counters, last visible source queue fence, CE/Window points, raw GPU timestamp and monotonic CPU/head IRQ observations. Missing reports/bootfb are unavailable, not a fabricated completed frame. Released counts scanout uses, not freed allocations.",
  "validation": {
    "kernel": "Existing display takeover group exercises the generic store with invalid/stale identities, malformed visible proof, monotonic bounds, duplicate retry, independent head keys, capacity and rebind invalidation. Real Kernel artifact builds; private SMP4 guest reads the optional API on bootfb and an unsupported head after existing native mode transitions.",
    "limits": "NVIDIA hardware responses remain modeled. No physical signal, visible output, latency, tearing or performance qualification; OssiGPU.txt remains OPEN. One short SMP4 guest, no broad or long-running suite.",
    "device": "Existing actual Device model asserts producer statistics against its real runtime CE/flip/head receipts, including render-only stages, old-image FINISHED, source fence identity, error Lost, Busy retry and a legacy display table. Previously integrated framepool and mode cleanup cases stay active.",
    "new_gate": false,
